{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1067884-noob-questions","id":1067884,"title":"Noob Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-24T18:53:32-07:00","id":1067884,"title":"Noob Questions","content":"So I am not too familiar with Wraith and I have a few questions. <br /> <br /> 1. Do wraiths replay the day they die and if so what is it called?<br /> 1.1: If they do replay their events can someone free them from the cycle and if so do they pass on or linger around?<br /> <br /> 2. What happens to Umbral Spirits if they end up in the underworld?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T19:05:07-07:00","id":1067886,"title":"","content":"Wraiths are those dead with enough of their wits about them to not be mindless; ghosts who endlessly repeat tasks or the events of their deaths are known as Drones, and are usually left alone until someone rounds them all up for soulforging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T19:33:01-07:00","id":1067890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1067884-noob-questions#post1067884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am not too familiar with Wraith and I have a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1. Do wraiths replay the day they die and if so what is it called?<br /> 1.1: If they do replay their events can someone free them from the cycle and if so do they pass on or linger around?<br /> <br /> 2. What happens to Umbral Spirits if they end up in the underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>1.1 Doing just that was a major part of Orpheus, the Wraith spin-off game. At least in the original book before PLOT happened. Since Orpheus is getting a section in Wraith20 we might see some of the &quot;redeem the Blips&quot; coming back. (It netted some really juicy rewards if you could get them to break out of their cycle...)<br /> <br /> 2. They probably starve....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T11:56:00-07:00","id":1070219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1067884-noob-questions?p=1067890#post1067890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. They probably starve....</div> </div> </div> </div>And go mad. Not necessarily in that order, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:14:20-07:00","id":1070434,"title":"","content":"It is very difficult for the spirits of the Middle Umbra to enter the Low Umbra and, even if they did, they can leave by Materializing into the Physical World and then returning to the Middle Umbra (the same would probably apply to High Umbra spirits in the Low Umbra). Of course, there are probably ways for others to keep spirits of the Middle Umbra trapped in the Low Umbra, but that probably requires a fair amount of mojo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T12:16:58-07:00","id":1070788,"title":"","content":"The Materialize charm isn't universal, though, so plenty of spirits would be trapped if they were unlucky enough to get to the Low Umbra in the first place. They can probably be soul forged though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:11:25-07:00","id":1070820,"title":"","content":"Is there somewhere it states that Materialize (et al. for the similar clutch of Charms) definitively works across the Shroud the same way it works across the Gauntlet? They aren't actually the same thing really. Even with Materialize, a spirit might find itself trapped. Or, if Embody is a clue, find Materialize to be less useful than they recall.<br /> <br /> Cue madness....<br /> <br /> Considering the existence of Puppetry and Inhabit, it's probably easier to use for the Possession Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}